Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> A hint in some recent posting let me find Patrick M�ller's Advent Calendar
> patch. First let me say that I find this a very nice idea!
>
> I inspected the patch code and got the impression that any of the 24 doors
> can be unlocked only if the respective day of the month is current. Is that
> observation correct? That would mean that a player who plays a whole game
> in just a few days won't see much of it; which is a pity.

Yes, that's how it works.

> In Real Life I occasionally missed to open the calendar "doors" some days,
> but of course I opened them afterwards, when I noticed, or when I returned
> back home. Wouldn't it be nice to be able, also in the patch, to open all
> doors of already passed days?

Yes, but think about someone starting a game late in December. This
player would get all the food and goodies up until that day.

Because of possible balance issues I made it to unlock only the door
corresponding to the current day.

I didn't think about it when doing the patch but a possibility would
be to only open up doors from the start date of the game until the
current day.

OTOH it's a magical advent calendar level. It doesn't need to resemble
exactly the real life item's behavior (and with enough preparations I
think it's even possible to steal stuff from the closets).


